From ff8931308767687c1fadfd19c6f49904a14e9ecd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:20:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(post): refuse a tool number above the machine tool
 table

The machine file can now state tooling.max_tool_number, the highest
tool number that the control's tool table holds. The reader refuses a
value that is not a whole number of 1 or more. The mirror carries it,
and scripts read it as machine.toolNumberMax.

The Fehlmann Picomax 55 states 254 (MP 7260 = 254). Both Heidenhain
posts refuse a higher tool number by name: Klartext with a script
error, DIN/ISO with a counted warning. A machine without the key keeps
the old behaviour.

Fixes #4087

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
